# Secrets and local state -- never commit.
.env.local
*.token
secrets.yaml

# The four reference repos are separate clones with their own history and their
# own licences. They are read as input and never committed here; the corpus is
# the derived artifact. Committing them would relicense nothing and would put
# four more .git trees inside this one.
/ressources/

# The unfiltered extraction. The committed `catalog/` holds facts for all four
# repos -- paths, ids, classes, vocabulary terms, entity identifiers -- and no
# field that can hold authored text. This directory holds the same records
# verbatim, including the aliases, display names, comments and YAML blocks of
# the two repos that grant nothing, and those are what a licence withholds
# rather than what it lets us keep. It exists so the local provenance gate can
# compare a shipped string against its source. It sits outside `catalog/`
# because every data file in `catalog/` must validate against a schema and this
# store is the one file the corpus validator is required to reject.
.local/

# Home Assistant runtime state for the dev container -- the database, logs,
# registries and the config onboarding writes. All of it is generated, none of
# it is authored, and it is ignored wholesale so a container run can never
# commit a token or a device registry. Our own configuration lives in this
# repository (`custom_components/`, `packs/`, `engine/`) and is never written
# here. It is not mounted yet either: the compose file currently mounts only
# this directory, localtime and dbus, and the mount arrives with the integration
# in a later phase.
docker/ha-config/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Node / panel
node_modules/
panel/dist/
